    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711">

                <pb facs="0934" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/8462</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Peruvian Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>The Government of Peru is certain that the United States Government is not
                    contemplating the possibility of intervening in the domestic affairs of
                    Nicaragua. The Government of Peru proclaims and maintains the absolute principle
                    of non-intervention by one State in the domestic affairs of another, in
                    conformity with the declaration adopted in article 8 of the Convention on Eights
                    and Duties of States, signed at the Seventh International Conference of American
                    States at Montevideo, December 26, 1933, with the signatures of Peru, the United
                    States and Nicaragua, and the express declarations which, with the approval of
                    the Continent, the Delegation of the United States made, on signing it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1936-06-04">June 4,
                            1936</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
